---
title: OAuth
description: How apps are authorized on NeoWorks. PKCE, scopes, consent and the account vault.
---

NeoWorks uses standard OAuth 2.0 with PKCE. Apps use the authorization code flow, and S256
code challenges are required.

## Consent

When an app asks for access, you are sent to the account vault. There you pick which data the
app may use. The vault then gives the app access to those nodes and signs a certificate for
that installation of the app.

The app's tokens are tied to its installation. The API treats a token with an installation
as that app, limited to what you granted, and a session in the vault as you.

## Scopes

Scopes name a collection and an action: `calendar:read`, `calendar:write`, `contacts:read`,
`contacts:write`, `photos:read`, `photos:write`, `files:read` and `files:write`, plus
`openid`, `profile` and `email`. A scope never gives more than the grants you approved.

## Tokens

Access tokens are short-lived signed JWTs. Refresh tokens rotate on use. The public keys for
verifying tokens are published at the JWKS endpoint advertised in the discovery document.

## Managing apps

You can see and revoke connected apps from your dashboard. Revoking an app ends its tokens
and removes its access to your data.
